## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates governance design capabilities for small remote teams, focusing on beginner-friendly processes that balance innovation with stability; emphasizes risk management, stakeholder communication, and scalable automation.

## Key Concepts
- Semantic versioning methodology
- Deprecation policy frameworks
- Automated compatibility testing
- Feature flag rollbacks
- Partner communication protocols

## Code Example
```javascript
// Version compatibility validator
function isCompatible(currentVersion, targetVersion) {
  const [cMA, cMi, cPa] = currentVersion.split('.').map(Number);
  const [tMA, tMi, tPa] = targetVersion.split('.').map(Number);

  // Major version changes are breaking
  if (cMA !== tMA) return false;

  // Minor version changes are backward compatible
  if (cMi > tMi) return false;

  return true;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This asks for a concrete governance approach to align many teams around data contracts, versioning, and regulatory constraints, a frequent real-world pain point in fintech.

## Key Concepts
- Contract driven development
- Data contracts and API versioning
- Cross team governance and automation
- Compliance and incident response

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal contract validation skeleton
function validateContract(data, contract) {
  for (const field of contract.requiredFields) {
    if (data[field] === undefined) return false;
  }
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure success and roll out across more teams?
- What are risks and mitigations for contract churn and migration?
